# acme-proxy client allow-list
#
# One entry per line: a single IP address or a CIDR subnet.
# Lines starting with '#' are comments; blank lines are ignored.
#
# The file is re-read whenever it changes on disk, so edits apply to
# the next request without restarting the daemon. It can also be edited from
# the dashboard (ACL tab), which validates entries before saving.
#
# Point ca.json at this file:
#   "acl": { "file": "/opt/acme-proxy/acl.txt" }
#
# NOTE: X-Forwarded-For is honored only when "trust_forwarded_for": true is
# set in the acl block (for reverse-proxy deployments). With it off (the
# default) the socket address is authoritative and cannot be spoofed.

# single hosts
192.0.2.10
198.51.100.7

# subnets
192.0.2.0/24
2001:db8:1234::/48
